# Runbook §6.1 — generated outputs and evidence must not appear as
# untracked files after the gate (bin/session-01-check.sh step 1).

.generated/*
!.generated/.gitkeep

evidence/*
!evidence/.gitkeep

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Session 2 operator inputs. These name a real host, real DNS, and a real
# provider organization, so only the redacted *.example.yaml forms are
# committed (runbook Session 2 §5.4).
#
# They are ignored rather than merely untracked because bin/session-01-check.sh
# step 1 fails on ANY untracked file, and these files live in the checkout on
# the deployment host where that gate also runs.
#
# A glob with a negation, rather than one line per project name (D1034).
#
# This was a list of the two names this repository's own operator happens to
# run, and its comment justified that: a bare glob would silently hide a future
# project.third.example.yaml that ought to be committed. The reasoning was
# sound and the consequence was not. host.yaml and capabilities.yaml are
# ignored generically and work for anybody; a THIRD project's manifest -- which
# is to say any adopter's -- landed as an untracked file, and step 1 of
# bin/session-01-check.sh fails on any untracked file while a dirty release
# makes a deploy refuse outright (D971). So the first act of adopting this
# product was to fork it and edit this file, which upstream then conflicts on
# at every merge.
#
# The negation keeps the property the old comment wanted. Note it is
# `*example.yaml` and NOT `*.example.yaml`: the latter fails to match
# `project.example.yaml` itself, because there is no segment before `.example`
# there. Measured with `git check-ignore -v`, not reasoned about.
#
# `/project.yaml` is separate and not redundant: `/project.*.yaml` requires a
# segment between the dots, so it does not match `project.yaml` -- which is
# exactly the name README.md's own quick-start tells a reader to create
# (D1035).
/host.yaml
/capabilities.yaml
/project.yaml
/project.*.yaml
!/project.*example.yaml

# Deployed documents an operator installs from the host to run `--mode external`.
#
# **Two of these were tracked for six sessions** (D730). `alpha-outputs.json` and
# `beta-outputs.json` sat in the repository root at `schema_version` 10,
# `deployed_through_session` 6, observed 2026-08-15 — and they did not validate
# against the current schema at all. Four operator guides name them as the path
# to pass to `--project-a-outputs`, so an external run from a fresh checkout
# measured a Session 6 deployment while believing it measured the current one.
# `MUST_AGREE` on `source_commit` refuses the merge, which is four steps from the
# cause.
#
# Ignored rather than merely deleted: the file an operator installs has this name
# by convention, and a stale observation in source control has the shape of the
# real thing under a filename that reads as current.
/*-outputs.json
